<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines to reject new oil-fired power plants.</title>
<headline>Philippines to reject new oil-fired power plants.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-08-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Department of Energy said on Monday it has stopped accepting applications for the construction and operation of diesel and bunker fuel-fired power plants.</p>
<p>In an administrative order signed Monday, Energy Secretary Francisco Viray said these kinds of power plants do not conform now with the government's long-term policy of reducing the country's dependence on oil, especially in power generation.</p>
<p>In 1992 when the country went through a severe electricity shortage crisis, the government had encouraged oil-fired power plants since they could be set up quickly.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 841-8937 fax 8176267</p>
